# Upstream binary release pinning manifest.
#
# Each line is a SHA256SUMS-compatible row: <hash>  <category>/<filename>
# Categories:
#   rustic/<target>/  → rustic upstream release artifact (extracted: rustic binary)
#   python/<target>/  → python-build-standalone install_only_stripped tarball
#   dvdisaster/src/   → dvdisaster RS03 source tarball (NOT extracted; the
#                       archive itself is bundled on the meta-volume so a
#                       future engineer can re-implement RS03 from the exact
#                       source that docs/DVDISASTER_RS03_FORMAT.md transcribes)
#
# Targets (six approved per docs/CROSS_PLATFORM_META_RFC.md §6 Q1):
#   x86_64-unknown-linux-musl       Linux x86_64 (static, replaces glibc target)
#   aarch64-unknown-linux-musl      Linux ARM64 (static; Pi 4/5, Asahi, Graviton)
#   armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf   Linux 32-bit ARM (Pi 1/2/3/Zero)
#   aarch64-apple-darwin            macOS Apple Silicon
#   x86_64-apple-darwin             macOS Intel
#   x86_64-pc-windows-gnu (rustic)  Windows (rustic's gnu variant)
#   x86_64-pc-windows-msvc (python) Windows (PBS's msvc variant — they don't ship gnu)
#
# Source URLs (regenerate this file by running recovery/scripts/fetch_upstream.sh):
#   https://github.com/rustic-rs/rustic/releases/download/v0.11.2/
#   https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases/download/20260510/
#   https://codeload.github.com/speed47/dvdisaster/tar.gz/refs/tags/v0.79.10-pl6

